<title>GERMANY: Siemens says dollar level could boost sales.</title>
<headline>Siemens says dollar level could boost sales.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The dollar's current strength could boost sales at Siemens AG two percent in the current business year, chief financial officer Karl-Hermann Baumann said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Baumann told the company's annual news conference the company had initially projected sales growth of four to five percent this year.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
